## Agents DevKits bridge

Progressive Context Kit remains the owner of project context, `.progressive/`
memory, phase state, completion records, and its context-loading sequence. Run
the PCK router first; do not create a second project-state or history system.

For a multi-step change or release check, use `.agents-devkits/ROUTING.md` only
to shortlist extra specialist workflows. Read a selected skill's `SKILL.md` on
demand. `AUTO` selects a justified boundary, `PROPOSE` announces and continues
unless redirected, and `ASK` requires an explicit request. These levels never
override PCK instructions, safety rules, or authorization requirements.

If a PCK project-local skill and a globally installed Agents DevKits skill have
the same name, use the PCK local skill. `agents-devkits.yaml` and
`.agents-devkits/` describe optional DevKits routing and verification only; they
do not own product intent, architecture, roadmap, phase status, or completion
records.
